{
  "id": "PPA-08",
  "title": "Specialized & Secondary Metabolism",
  "subtitle": "Phenylpropanoid entry, monolignol lignin polymerization, and anthocyanin flavonoid branching",
  "caption": "Specialized plant secondary metabolism. Phenylalanine is channeled into core phenylpropanoids by PAL, C4H, and 4CL, generating activated 4-coumaroyl-CoA. From this central branchpoint, flux bifurcates into: (1) monolignols via CCR and CAD for cell-wall lignification; and (2) flavonoids via Chalcone Synthase (CHS/TT4), CHI, F3H, and DFR, culminating in vacuolar anthocyanin and proanthocyanidin sequestration via GST transporter TT19.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
